  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For \\(x = 7,\\) which of the following is the smallest?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x+1} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x-1} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{x}{6} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{x+1}{6} \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substituting \\(x = 7\\) gives the five values \\(\\dfrac{6}{7},\\) \\(\\dfrac{6}{8},\\) \\(1,\\) \\(\\dfrac{7}{6},\\) and \\(\\dfrac{4}{3}.\\)\n\nThe first two are the only values less than \\(1.\\) Because they have the same numerator, the fraction with the larger denominator is smaller. Thus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(x = 7\\) first.",
        "With equal numerators, compare denominators."
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
